This confirms a provider-schema/runtime-schema mismatch.

Make the smallest contract-alignment fix.

Requirements:

1. &#x20;Keep the runtime Zod/schema constraints unchanged.&#x20;
2. &#x20;Update the JSON Schema sent to OpenAI so it enforces the same Investigator constraints as the runtime schema.&#x20;
3. &#x20;At minimum align:&#x20;
   - &#x20;hypothesis ID pattern `^hyp-`&#x20;
   - &#x20;hypothesis count `1–3`&#x20;
   - &#x20;confidence range `0–1`&#x20;
   - &#x20;non-empty strings where runtime requires them&#x20;
   - `request_reproduction.hypothesisId`&#x20;
   - `finish_inconclusive.explanation`&#x20;
   - &#x20;any other provider/runtime mismatch already identified&#x20;
4. &#x20;Correlate each action discriminator with its correct argument shape so an action cannot receive arguments intended for another action.&#x20;
5. &#x20;Do not weaken runtime validation.&#x20;
6. &#x20;Do not change:&#x20;
   - `baseline-v2`&#x20;
   - &#x20;benchmark artifacts&#x20;
   - &#x20;ground truth&#x20;
   - &#x20;Investigator responsibilities&#x20;
   - &#x20;agentic orchestration semantics&#x20;
7. &#x20;Determine whether `investigator-v1` needs a version bump.&#x20;
   - &#x20;If its text does not change, keep `investigator-v1`.&#x20;
   - &#x20;Treat this as provider-schema contract alignment rather than a prompt change.&#x20;
8. &#x20;Add regression tests proving:&#x20;
   - `"H1"` is rejected by the provider schema representation / schema consistency test;&#x20;
   - `"hyp-1"` is accepted;&#x20;
   - &#x20;confidence outside 0–1 is rejected;&#x20;
   - &#x20;zero or more than three hypotheses is rejected;&#x20;
   - &#x20;action/argument discriminator mismatches are rejected;&#x20;
   - &#x20;provider JSON schema and runtime schema stay aligned for all Investigator action variants.&#x20;
9. &#x20;If practical, add a schema-consistency test/helper so future changes to the runtime contract cannot silently diverge from the provider JSON schema again.&#x20;

Run:
```arduino
npm run typecheck
npm test
